# Stand on the bottom level of the dungeon, levitating over a chasm, and SAVE
# there, so the state can be frozen into a character fixture. (bd inc-30ps)
#
#   INCURSION_LEVITATE_CHASM=1 \
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/levitate-bottom-save.keys 1
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. tools/keys/levitate-bottom.keys builds this same situation
# and never saves it, so every run re-generates depth 10 from whatever module
# is on disk at that moment -- and generation consumes the shared random
# stream, so an unrelated change to src/ that makes different rolls on the way
# down can hand back a depth 10 with no chasm at all. That happened to
# tools/check_dungeonmap_bounds.sh under inc-30ps: the combat rework changed
# how many rolls generation makes before depth 10, so seed 5, which used to
# produce a chasm, stopped producing one (0 fall squares on this branch,
# INCURSION_CHASM_WALK probe). Seed 1 still produces one here (233 fall
# squares) and is what this script freezes. A LOADED save does not
# regenerate, so freezing this moment lets the check outlive an unrelated
# combat change. See tools/fixtures/README.md and bd inc-1fjk for why a save
# survives a module change where a generated level does not.
#
# THE WALK IS UNCHANGED FROM levitate-bottom.keys, and for the same reason:
# the nine wizard depth jumps below are the route
# docs/evidence/inc-x9i/observed-routes/to-bottom-level.keys took on
# 2026-08-18, and map content is NOT a property of the seed alone. A straight
# descent on seed 3362 produced a depth 10 with ZERO chasm squares where the
# survey recorded 282. Do not shorten this file.
#
# INCURSION_LEVITATE_CHASM grants LEVITATION and stands the player ON a chasm
# square on arrival at the deepest level (src/Feature.cpp). It manufactures no
# terrain; a potion of levitation and a walk would reach the same state. It
# only needs to fire during THIS generating run -- the fixture then carries
# levitation and the chasm-standing position in the save itself, so a session
# that loads it later needs no probe hook at all.
#
# ESC b is the System Menu's [b] Save and Continue (src/Player.cpp:843), and
# it is the only save the game offers that does not also end the session.
# READ THE WARNING IN tools/keys/save-continue.keys BEFORE MOVING IT: ESC
# opens that menu rather than cancelling anything, [a] is Save and Quit, and a
# stray ESC therefore ends the run and still exits 0. The @expect below is the
# guard against exactly that.
#
# THERE IS NO @quit HERE, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE -- see the same note in
# tools/keys/lizardfolk-monk-save.keys. @quit is Save and Quit, which would
# write the save a second time and shuffle this one off to a .backup file.

@include chargen.keys

@dump:arrival

w y p "2" ENTER
PGDN*3 PGDN*3 UP*3 PGUP*2 END*4 END*4 s .*2
w p "3" ENTER
PGUP*2 UP*2 LEFT*4 LEFT*3 HOME*5 PGUP*1 s .*2
w p "4" ENTER
LEFT*1 HOME*3 UP*2 END*1 RIGHT*1 UP*5 s .*2
w p "5" ENTER
PGUP*3 RIGHT*4 HOME*5 END*2 UP*5 RIGHT*5 s .*2
w p "6" ENTER
UP*5 END*1 RIGHT*1 LEFT*4 LEFT*1 UP*5 s .*2
w p "7" ENTER
RIGHT*4 PGUP*2 RIGHT*2 UP*3 PGDN*1 HOME*5 s .*2
w p "8" ENTER
RIGHT*3 LEFT*4 HOME*1 PGDN*1 END*3 END*1 s .*2
w p "9" ENTER
DOWN*3 END*1 LEFT*5 PGUP*3 DOWN*2 DOWN*3 s .*2
w p "10" ENTER

# The wizard depth change leaves a dialog box (MO_DIALOG) on the screen, and
# one key dismisses it.
ESC
@dump:on-bottom

# Save and continue, rather than asking to descend -- that is now the CHECK's
# job, run fresh against the loaded fixture.
ESC                     # System Menu -- and NOT a cancel; see the header
@expect "System Menu"   # refuse to press a letter into any other screen
b                       # [b] Save and Continue
@dump:saved
